      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12842681::web::036::4_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing at approximately 900°C for 2 hours in an inert atmosphere is a suitable homogenization treatment for the starting alloy.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Homogenization will make Al, Cr, and Ti more uniformly distributed.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12842681::web::036::4_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A more uniform elemental distribution will facilitate formation of a continuous, coherent, and adherent mixed oxide scale.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The uniform mixed oxide scale will resist spallation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The uniform mixed oxide scale will reduce degradation under both oxidizing and reducing gas exposures.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
